			"Message": "build(Project): Coordinate Element submodule updates across 6 components\n\nSynchronize all 6 Element submodules with the following changes:\n\n- **Mountain:** Add extension metadata passthrough (Atom TH1) — 14 new fields to ExtensionDescriptionStateDTO for VS Code package.json metadata (Categories, DisplayName, Description, Keywords, Repository, Bugs, Homepage, License, Icon, AiKey, ExtensionKind, Capabilities, ExtensionDependencies, ExtensionPack). Implement IPC round-trip for applyEdit/showTextDocument (Atom T1) using request/response pattern instead of fire-and-forget events. Add Node version checking (Atom N1) — ResolveNodeBinary queries `node --version` and logs resolved version with warning for outdated major versions. Add compile-time PostHog config (Atom P2) via env! macro in build.rs. Add IPC logging with paired entry/exit lines for latency diagnosis.\n\n- **Sky:** Add round-trip IPC handlers (Atom T1) for workspace/applyEdit and window/showTextDocument with RequestIdentifier tracking. Implement UI dialog round-trip replies (Atom Q1) for show-message-request, show-input-box-request, show-quick-pick-request. Add PostHog configuration via environment (Atom PH1/PH2) with client-side rate limiting and batch window. Add extension runtime dependency installer (Atom S1) that runs `npm install --production` for extensions with runtime deps.\n\n- **Wind:** Add PostHog telemetry bridge (Source/Telemetry/PostHogBridge.ts) that reuses Sky's window.posthog instance in webview or falls back to HTTP POST in Node.js. Tags events with $tier: \"wind\" for analytics filtering.\n\n- **Common:** Bump pnpm/action-setup from 6.0.0 to 6.0.3 (dependabot).\n\n- **Maintain:** Replace em-dashes with hyphens in CHANGELOG and code comments for consistent formatting.\n\n- **Cocoon:** Submodule updated to 38b5cb557b5de41dd3164ed71b46fdafc09aac01.\n\nThis coordinated update delivers IPC round-trip reliability for editor operations, extension metadata filtering support, frontend PostHog telemetry, and Node version diagnostics.",
